    "research": {
      "notes": "**USO (United States Oil Fund, LP), 2026-09-29 to 2026-10-29.** USO is a commodity-pool ETF, so it has no earnings guidance, sell-side coverage or customers in the usual sense. I found no sources for several topics below, and I say so where that applies.\n\n**1. Guidance / results**\n- There is no guidance. USO is a passive WTI futures fund. Nothing material found for this topic.\n- USO closed at $166.57 on 2026-10-28. It is up 11% over the past month and up 133.3% over the past year. — 2026-10-28 — https://www.stocktitan.net/overview/USO/\n- The 52-week high was $169.96 on 10/23/26. — 2026-10-23 — https://www.cnbc.com/quotes/USO\n- The fund files monthly account statements on Form 8-K. The July 2026 statement showed net income of $414.7M. — period ended 2026-07-31 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001327068/000110465926102786/tm2623039d1_ex99-1.htm\n- The August 2026 statement showed net income of $84.0M. — period ended 2026-08-31 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001327068/000110465926111777/tm2625422d1_ex99-1.htm\n- StockTitan lists a Form 8-K filed on 2026-10-20 under a headline about a \"$270M May 2026 loss\". I could not check the filing text, so treat that as unverified. — filing date 2026-10-20 — https://www.stocktitan.net/overview/USO/\n\n**2. Analyst actions**\n- I found no upgrades, downgrades, initiations or price-target changes from any named firm. Coverage aggregators show no analyst price targets. — date unknown — https://www.tipranks.com/etf/uso\n- StockInvest.us, a quantitative technical model rather than a brokerage, upgraded USO from Buy to Strong Buy Candidate. — 2026-10-23 — https://stockinvest.us/stock/USO\n\n**3. Litigation / regulation**\n- I found no new lawsuits, investigations or fines in the window.\n- The June 2026 10-Q still describes an earlier CFTC order against USCF, the general partner. It covers April 22 to June 12, 2020 and concerns fraud and advertising findings. This is not new. — 2020-04-22 (conduct period start) — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1327068/000110465926092623/uso-20260630x10q.htm\n\n**4. Customer concentration**\n- This does not apply to a fund. I found no customer news.\n- A 13F-based filing shows the largest holders in the March 2026 quarter were market makers and banks: Susquehanna, Citadel Securities, Jane Street and Goldman Sachs. Most of their positions were options. — 2026-03-31 — https://www.signalbloom.ai/13f/ticker/USO\n\n**5. Insider activity**\n- I found no Form 4 purchases or sales with a transaction date in the window.\n- StockTitan shows 2 Form 4s and a Form 3/A in USO's recent filings. The Form 3/A (2026-10-20 filing) concerns HRT Financial LP short sales of 88,454 shares. Transaction dates were not shown. — transaction date unknown — https://www.stocktitan.net/overview/USO/\n- GuruFocus cites net insider buying over 12 months of $23.4M against sales of $14.7M. This is an aggregator figure with no transaction dates, and I could not verify it. — date unknown — https://www.gurufocus.com/news/9126260/october-2026-oil-inventory-data-highlights-market-dynamics-impacting-uso-united-states-oil-fund\n- USCF held no USO shares at 2026-06-30. — 2026-06-30 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1327068/000110465926092623/uso-20260630x10q.htm\n\n**6. Product / competitive**\n- USCF announced on 2026-10-09 that it will liquidate ZSB, WTIB, USE, USG and UDI. Trading in WTIB and USE halts on 2026-11-06, with liquidation around 2026-11-13. USO is not affected. — 2026-10-09 — https://www.kucoin.com/news/flash/uscf-announces-product-line-restructuring-and-fund-liquidations (original press release, syndicated: https://theprescotttimes.com/online_features/press_releases/uscf-announces-changes-to-product-line/article_9e712955-d709-5e6d-b12c-8096d0947a26.html)\n- Pricing: the 10-Q says USCF's management fee is 0.45% of NAV. — 2026-06-30 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1327068/000110465926092623/uso-20260630x10q.htm\n- PortfoliosLab shows USO's total expense ratio at 0.86%. Cheaper oil ETFs include BBLS (0.32%, inception Aug 2026, about $8M AUM), OILK (0.69%) and DBO (0.78%). — 2026-08 (BBLS inception) — https://portfolioslab.com/symbol/USO/alternatives\n- Market drivers:\n  - Crude inventories fell 1.89M barrels against an expected build of 81,000 barrels. — 2026-10-28 — https://www.gurufocus.com/news/9147683/crude-oil-inventories-drop-sharply-uso-reacts-amid-mixed-gasoline-and-distillate-stock-changes\n  - USO fell 2.61% intraday on Houthi attacks on Saudi facilities and Gulf tensions. — 2026-10-20 — https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/10/62470714/united-states-oil-dips-whats-going-on\n  - GuruFocus, citing the EIA report, put the market cap at $1.84B. — 2026-10-28 — https://www.gurufocus.com/news/9147683/crude-oil-inventories-drop-sharply-uso-reacts-amid-mixed-gasoline-and-distillate-stock-changes",
